## Key Concepts
- Multimodal fusion strategies and on-device inference
- Privacy-preserving cloud inference with encrypted fallback
- Latency budgeting and threshold calibration across languages
- Model explainability and fairness/drift monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
function fuse(textModel, visualModel, audioModel) {
  // Attention-weighted fusion of modality scores
  const textScore = textModel.predict(textInput);
  const visualScore = visualModel.predict(videoFrames);
  const audioScore = audioModel.predict(audioStream);

  // Attention-based calibration head
  const weights = attentionLayer([textScore, visualScore, audioScore]);
  return weightedSum([textScore, visualScore, audioScore], weights);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This task asks for a practical, beginner-friendly NLP feature that is directly useful in real-world chat apps: extracting and standardizing time references across languages, with on-device constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Time expression parsing across EN/ES/DE
- On-device inference with WebAssembly
- Normalization to ISO 8601 and confidence signaling

## Code Example

```javascript
function normalizeTime(text) {
  const idx = text.indexOf(":");
  if (idx > 0 && idx < text.length - 1) {
    const before = text[idx - 1];
    const after = text[idx + 1];
    if (before >= '0' && before <= '9' && after >= '0' && after <= '9') {
      const start = Math.max(0, idx - 2);
      const end = Math.min(text.length, idx + 3);
      return text.substring(start, end);
    }
  }
  return null;
}
```

